lisa-design:
- slack-preview needs no GitHub token (sample data only), so the workflow mints no app token; contents: read only.
- With --which all, a sample whose SLACK_CHANNEL_* variable is unset is skipped with a ::warning:: (so one missing channel doesn't block the others); naming a sample whose variable is unset fails; no channel at all fails.
- Edits wait --pause (default 10s) via an injected sleep so tests run instantly; the releases sample posts the board at stage 1 and edits it 3 times (stage 2, stage 3, finished) with one thread reply per edit.
- Thread replies are previews too (Preview() on every call), so nothing a viewer sees looks like a real event.
- --dry-run swaps in slackkit.Fake and prints the calls; it needs no token.

